{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "version": "0.13.0",
  "candidateTag": "v0.13.0-prealpha.3",
  "summary": "This release uses stock OMP v19.1.1 as its engineering baseline. The 14 changelog entries below record the changes since v0.12.0. Historical receipts do not qualify these bytes.",
  "highlights": "- This release uses stock OMP v19.1.1 as its engineering baseline. The 14 changelog entries below record the changes since v0.12.0. Historical receipts do not qualify these bytes.\n- When a new Tern session's command ends before OMP can be opened, OMP Sessions points to the kept-open tab instead of waiting for the adoption timeout.\n- Move the toolchain and the release runtime floor to Bun 1.4.5, a Bun security release: installing this release needs Bun 1.4.5 or newer. Earlier releases keep their qualification.\n- Adopt new Tern sessions sooner by overlapping preflight checks and refreshing OMP discovery with bounded backoff after Tern reports the session-file basename.\n- Run independent `omp-gateway doctor` probes concurrently to shorten diagnostics.\n- Request the first session list alongside fleet configuration to show the directory sooner.\n- Advance the independent host engineering baseline to stock OMP 19.1.1 with measured source and native pins; retain the minimum host and published qualification.\n- Refresh the embedded client and wire dependency to exact OMP 19.1.1 source: rejoin instead of going live when a later welcome fails to apply, keep finished streaming Markdown blocks' DOM, nest bash tool-command cards, show brief intent labels and answerless web-search excerpts; keep View guards on the new resume and deliver-queue senders and older hosts' xd:// and artifact:// rendering.\n- Send navigations and same-origin `/api/` requests directly to the network in browsers with service-worker static routing, so those requests do not wait for the worker to start.\n- Serve static text assets with Brotli or gzip, compressed in memory at startup, and revalidate unhashed shell files with `ETag`. API and bootstrap responses and the release archive are unchanged. Text assets and shell files no longer answer byte-range requests.\n- Leave the session rows in place when a directory refresh changes nothing. A tap that spanned such a refresh was dropped and keyboard focus could move. A refresh that changes a row still replaces the list. Row actions now use the current session generation and request.\n- Run the advisory Percy upload with the CLI's release check disabled, so a newer `@percy/cli` release no longer prints the update warning that failed every finalized upload.\n- Keep Tern session creation available when a pane in the window has a long title or argument, or a tab is deeply split; such unread metadata no longer invalidates the whole inspection.\n- Add a `credentials_only` mode to the droplet qualification workflow. It stops after the secret and Tailscale key preflights, so expired hosted credentials are found before a campaign starts.\n- Keep the Android Push coordinator-restart phase from thawing every frozen app: Play Services state is read only after a restart clear has failed, and a restarted worker fails typed.",
  "combinations": "| role | combination |\n|---|---|\n| Linux host | Run 45682551751 succeeded (https://github.com/carrythroughsystems/omp-session-gateway/actions/runs/45682551751); OS/kernel versions and migration counts are not exported. |\n| macOS host | VirtualMac2,1, macOS 27.0 arm64; doctor 18/18, rollback 23/23; native addon c2afb0d332e6f8f04ecd05fafe0b5838ca47c5748a9ed9d150de0a6db67f2cf7. |\n| Windows host | Windows x86-64 build 26100; 4 CPUs, 8186 MiB; Administrator upgrade/rollback from v0.12.0 and fresh standard-account lifecycle; interactive logon, not unattended boot. |\n| Chrome and Chromium | Pixel 8 Pro, Android 17, Chrome 158.0.8127.42; BrowserStack, tunnel 8.9: Galaxy S26 (16.0.0, chrome 152.0.7977.54) |\n| Safari and WebKit | TestingBot, tunnel 4.9: iPhone Air (26.2, safari 26.2); TestingBot, tunnel 4.9: iPad (9th generation) (26.6, safari 26.6) |\n| Android | Pixel 8 Pro, Android 17, Chrome 158.0.8127.42; BrowserStack, tunnel 8.9: Galaxy S26 (16.0.0, chrome 152.0.7977.54) |\n| iPhone and iPad | TestingBot, tunnel 4.9: iPhone Air (26.2, safari 26.2); TestingBot, tunnel 4.9: iPad (9th generation) (26.6, safari 26.6) |",
  "stableRollback": "The selected predecessor is v0.12.0. Gateway rollback does not switch or restart the separately running OMP process. This release uses stock OMP v19.1.1. rollback --to selects only retained runtimes. Preserve configuration and readiness-token state; see docs/UPGRADE_ROLLBACK.md for predecessor compatibility and stopped-service recovery.",
  "changesToTest": "- When a new Tern session's command ends before OMP can be opened, OMP Sessions points to the kept-open tab instead of waiting for the adoption timeout.\n- Move the toolchain and the release runtime floor to Bun 1.4.5, a Bun security release: installing this release needs Bun 1.4.5 or newer. Earlier releases keep their qualification.\n- Adopt new Tern sessions sooner by overlapping preflight checks and refreshing OMP discovery with bounded backoff after Tern reports the session-file basename.\n- Run independent `omp-gateway doctor` probes concurrently to shorten diagnostics.\n- Request the first session list alongside fleet configuration to show the directory sooner.\n- Advance the independent host engineering baseline to stock OMP 19.1.1 with measured source and native pins; retain the minimum host and published qualification.\n- Refresh the embedded client and wire dependency to exact OMP 19.1.1 source: rejoin instead of going live when a later welcome fails to apply, keep finished streaming Markdown blocks' DOM, nest bash tool-command cards, show brief intent labels and answerless web-search excerpts; keep View guards on the new resume and deliver-queue senders and older hosts' xd:// and artifact:// rendering.\n- Send navigations and same-origin `/api/` requests directly to the network in browsers with service-worker static routing, so those requests do not wait for the worker to start.\n- Serve static text assets with Brotli or gzip, compressed in memory at startup, and revalidate unhashed shell files with `ETag`. API and bootstrap responses and the release archive are unchanged. Text assets and shell files no longer answer byte-range requests.\n- Leave the session rows in place when a directory refresh changes nothing. A tap that spanned such a refresh was dropped and keyboard focus could move. A refresh that changes a row still replaces the list. Row actions now use the current session generation and request.\n- Run the advisory Percy upload with the CLI's release check disabled, so a newer `@percy/cli` release no longer prints the update warning that failed every finalized upload.\n- Keep Tern session creation available when a pane in the window has a long title or argument, or a tab is deeply split; such unread metadata no longer invalidates the whole inspection.\n- Add a `credentials_only` mode to the droplet qualification workflow. It stops after the secret and Tailscale key preflights, so expired hosted credentials are found before a campaign starts.\n- Keep the Android Push coordinator-restart phase from thawing every frozen app: Play Services state is read only after a restart clear has failed, and a restarted worker fails typed.\n- Qualify stock OMP v19.1.1 on every host lane. Requalify all thirteen lanes, including session-lifecycle and Push-triage scenarios, on these exact signed bytes; historical receipts and canaries do not transfer.",
  "plannedBoundary": "- Planned qualification: Debian 13 x86-64; macOS 27.0 (26A428) arm64 in a Virtualization.framework guest (VirtualMac2,1, ADR-033); a disposable Windows Server 2025 host (the Administrator lifecycle and a fresh standard-user install); Chrome on the physical Pixel 10 Pro, including its background-Push lane; and real iPhone, iPad, and Galaxy devices in TestingBot's cloud. Every lane must pass against these exact signed bytes before stable promotion; the plan is not evidence.",
  "candidateRollback": "The selected predecessor is v0.12.0; pruning keeps it installed as the recorded rollback target. Gateway rollback does not switch or restart OMP. Historical fork-era recovery is documented separately in docs/UPGRADE_ROLLBACK.md.",
